{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style","id":435331,"title":"The Pure, 2e-style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T23:03:22-07:00","id":435331,"title":"The Pure, 2e-style","content":"From <b>WtF2e</b>:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">This section assumes a pack of Forsaken includes Uratha, Wolf-Blooded, humans, and a totem. That's not the whole story. Some packs try to get closer to Wolf or Moon, bringing in wolves or spirits to their fold. These packs are more common among the Pure \u2014 the Fire-Touched bring spirits into their packs, while the Predator Kings boast of canine packmates. Some Forsaken take the same path, but they're rare.</span><br /> <br /> OK; we definitely need a revised book for the Pure Tribes, if only to address these unusual packmates in more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T00:05:02-07:00","id":435399,"title":"","content":"I hope the Predator Kings have a second unique Gift (in addition to Savagery), that includes a Giant Wolf form - I'm not saying bring back Primal Form in its entirety (the changed healing rules for Gauru form make that a bit overkill), but the giant wolf form to hunt other werewolves and humans was a good shtick for them to specialize in.<br /> <br /> Then I'd give them Strength &amp; Stealth as their other two Gifts, since that a) fits very well, and b) lets the Blood Talons and Hunters-in-Darkness maintain a unique specialty each (Rage &amp; Nature).<br /> <br /> <br /> The changes to Harmony means that the whole cycle-of-sin-and-penance and the related Rites need to be completely revamped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:39:53-07:00","id":435467,"title":"","content":"Hell I bet they just reinforce the hell out of fathers form with merits. Make it an absolute beast even without the gauru healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:12:44-07:00","id":435550,"title":"","content":"You'll note there's some rather more significant implications about new aspects to the Pure in their write-up in the Prey chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:17:12-07:00","id":435555,"title":"","content":"In Prey chapter there is mentioned that Pure Tribes are having &quot;non-monster&quot; Scared Prey - they Hunt <i>ideology</i>, not beings. What are proper Sacred Prey they hunt? Text is bit unclear in this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:33:54-07:00","id":435565,"title":"","content":"They hunt those who offend their particular ideology, as opposed to hunting ideology itself. What each Tribe chooses to go after is exactly as indicated in their Prey write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What specifically do you want to know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:01:02-07:00","id":435569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435399#post435399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the Predator Kings have a second unique Gift (in addition to Savagery), that includes a Giant Wolf form - I'm not saying bring back Primal Form in its entirety (the changed healing rules for Gauru form make that a bit overkill), but the giant wolf form to hunt other werewolves and humans was a good shtick for them to specialize in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly see that as necessary; there are easier alternatives.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe one of the benefits of being in the Tribe is easier access to Favored Form for Urshul and/or Urhan, and it is always at the expense of Hishu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:09:33-07:00","id":435577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435565#post435565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What each Tribe chooses to go after is exactly as indicated in their Prey write-up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> What specifically do you want to know?</div> </div> </div> </div>One word short of it? Like Forsaken Tribes hunt Werewolves, Hosts, Humans, Claimed and Spirits. I preper presentation about 2ed for our local RPG club - the Pure Tribes shorthand would be gladly used for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:16:08-07:00","id":435579,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a fetish in one of the books that made all a werewolf's non-human forms bigger and nastier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:24:23-07:00","id":435588,"title":"","content":"The one-word shorthand for what the Pure hunt? 'Infidels'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:43:42-07:00","id":435625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435588#post435588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one-word shorthand for what the Pure hunt? 'Infidels'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was hoping for something like:<ul><li><b>Fire-Touches:</b> Dishonest</li> <li><b>Ivory Claws:</b> Impure</li> <li><b>Predator Kings:</b> Weak</li> </ul>Description that could point on too Forsaken with easy, but not only - that even some humans or other monsters could work as Prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:47:29-07:00","id":435627,"title":"","content":"Well, each tribe should have their own particular brand of infidel to specialise in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:59:50-07:00","id":435635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435625#post435625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping for something like:<ul><li><b>Fire-Touches:</b> Dishonest</li> <li><b>Ivory Claws:</b> Impure</li> <li><b>Predator Kings:</b> Weak</li> </ul><br /> Description that could point on too Forsaken with easy, but not only - that even some humans or other monsters could work as Prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the Pure's sacred prey explained in the Prey chapter already indicates. The Pure have broader sacred prey concepts that can apply to various types of creature but, obviously, particularly tend to be relevant to the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I can't really make, for example, the Fire-Touched Sacred Prey of 'those who they see as dishonoring and disrespecting' the Shadow any clearer <i>and</i> shrink it down to one word :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:06:12-07:00","id":435640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435569#post435569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't particularly see that as necessary; there are easier alternatives.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe one of the benefits of being in the Tribe is easier access to Favored Form for Urshul and/or Urhan, and it is always at the expense of Hishu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to say they didn't really need a Gift for it because they can just stack Favored Form, Living Weapon and Fortified Form on Urshul, but you sniped me there!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435625#post435625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was hoping for something like:<ul><li><b>Fire-Touches:</b> Dishonest</li> <li><b>Ivory Claws:</b> Impure</li> <li><b>Predator Kings:</b> Weak</li> </ul><br /> Description that could point on too Forsaken with easy, but not only - that even some humans or other monsters could work as Prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure all hunt Forsaken by virtue of their bias, and likewise for humans. But the specific things they look for in prey are not quite that easily summarized. It'd be more accurate to say the Fire-Touched hunt the disrespectful (to the Shadow), the Predator Kings the dishonorable (to the Hunt), and the Ivory Claws the unfaithful (to their Lineage).<br /> <br /> Though Chris puts it really well in a nutshell when he says they hunt the Infidels (by their arbitrary standards), I feel like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:14:42-07:00","id":435650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435399#post435399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changes to Harmony means that the whole cycle-of-sin-and-penance and the related Rites need to be completely revamped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; the pure don\u2019t seem to care much about Harmony in general. To the extent that they do, it\u2019s solely because of practical considerations. I wouldn\u2019t mind if 2e\u2019s Pure Tribes got the equivalent of Gifts of the Moon (but per Tribe rather than per Auspice), with the Predator Kings getting something in there that mitigates the drawbacks of high Harmony and the Fire-Touched getting something to mitigate low Harmony. E.g., each has a way to retain the shapeshifting benefits that moderate Harmony provides even as they approach their preferred extreme. Ideally, these exemptions from the usual drawbacks would be replaced by <i>other</i> drawbacks, of a nature that the Pure probably wouldn\u2019t mind but the Forsaken probably <i>would</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:17:15-07:00","id":435653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435627#post435627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, each tribe should have their own particular brand of infidel to specialise in.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:18:31-07:00","id":435654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435650#post435650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; the pure don\u2019t seem to care much about Harmony in general. To the extent that they do, it\u2019s solely because of practical considerations. I wouldn\u2019t mind if 2e\u2019s Pure Tribes got the equivalent of Gifts of the Moon (but per Tribe rather than per Auspice), with the Predator Kings getting something in there that mitigates the drawbacks of high Harmony and the Fire-Touched getting something to mitigate low Harmony. E.g., each has a way to retain the shapeshifting benefits that moderate Harmony provides even as they approach their preferred extreme. Ideally, these exemptions from the usual drawbacks would be replaced by <i>other</i> drawbacks, of a nature that the Pure probably wouldn\u2019t mind but the Forsaken probably <i>would</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the savagery of the Predator Kings I would see them as very low-Harmony as well, not high-Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:22:02-07:00","id":435657,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Ivory Claws strike me as the most susceptible to leaning fleshwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:23:09-07:00","id":435658,"title":"","content":"The Predator Kings are vowed to &quot;Honor Nothing Of Human Craft&quot; though. Why would they have particularly high Harmony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:25:28-07:00","id":435660,"title":"","content":"Review the nature of Harmony in 2e: \u201chigh Harmony\u201d doesn\u2019t mean \u201charmonious\u201d anymore; it means \u201cbiased toward the Flesh\u201d. Likewise, \u201clow Harmony\u201d means \u201cbiased toward the Spirit\u201d. If you want to avoid both extremes, you aim for Harmony 5.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And \u201cFlesh\u201d doesn\u2019t necessarily mean \u201chuman\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:27:47-07:00","id":435662,"title":"","content":"Yes. So why would they have high Harmony? <i>My question stands.</i><br /> <br /> It does lean in part towards human behaviors though. And Predator Kings are likely the furthest werewolves from humanity, so that would naturally reflect on their Harmony and greater distance from Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-10-2015, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:30:55-07:00","id":435664,"title":"","content":"Looking at the standard breaking points it would seem to come down to how silver-happy they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:31:10-07:00","id":435665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435660#post435660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Review the nature of Harmony in 2e: \u201chigh Harmony\u201d doesn\u2019t mean \u201charmonious\u201d anymore; it means \u201cbiased toward the Flesh\u201d. Likewise, \u201clow Harmony\u201d means \u201cbiased toward the Spirit\u201d. If you want to avoid both extremes, you aim for Harmony 5.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And \u201cFlesh\u201d doesn\u2019t necessarily mean \u201chuman\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>You break towards Spirit for killing humans and wolves, eating human or wolf flesh, and throwing yourself into things that make you a predatory monster. One of the breaking points toward Flesh at low-Harmony includes eating processed food, which is something Predator Kings are never supposed to do.<br /> <br /> Predator Kings are all about those things, so it makes more sense that they tend towards the lower ranges of Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:32:30-07:00","id":435668,"title":"","content":"Because they strike me as being biased toward the Flesh. Wolf rather than Man, granted; but still Flesh rather than Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:34:31-07:00","id":435669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435668#post435668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they strike me as being biased toward the Flesh. Wolf rather than Man, granted; but still Flesh rather than Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like for you to break your reasoning down, then, because my points above seem to suggest the exact opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:42:15-07:00","id":435691,"title":"","content":"To be fair this is at least partially the book conflating &quot;wolfy&quot; and &quot;spirit&quot; somewhat. <br /> <br /> Still, I guess it would be an interesting thought experiment to ponder what wolf-centric breaking point towards flesh would be. In case someone wants to get their WtA on and have some werewolves who hail from the canine side of things, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:31:52-07:00","id":436052,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading Second Edition but I decided to throw in my opinion anyway. While I think that its an interesting idea to have the Pure define their tribal prey in such a different way from the Forsaken I think that some of them don't work for me. I kind of like the ideas of the Fire-touched and Ivory Claws hunting their kind of ideological opposites but I don't really like the vibe that the Predator Kings would hunt the weak.<br /> <br /> This is how I would run it.<br /> <br /> Fire-touched: Unbelievers (those who do not accept the truth of the Pure, shouldn't be very different here)<br /> Predator Kings: Rivals (I kind of dislike that they would be nothing more than bullies and better like the idea that they'll hunt whatever creature can possibly make a cause to challenge their position in the top, be it spirits, Forsaken, humans or other shifters, and so brutually killing off all competition as it comes)<br /> Ivory Claws: Impure (I would kind of imagine that they have a special hatred for the magath (if they are still part of the setting...) and whatever other creature that the Ivory Claws can consider to be impure in soime fashion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:46:41-07:00","id":436060,"title":"","content":"The Predator Kings <i>don't</i> hunt the 'weak' as their sacred prey <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The three sacred prey choices of the new Pure are all in their write-up in the Prey section <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:07:43-07:00","id":436084,"title":"","content":"Yeah we've been throwing a lot of opinions around, but their real sacred prey seems to be as follows:<br /> <br /> Ivory Claws - Those who do not honor their lineage.<br /> Predator Kings - Those who fail to appropriately honor the hunt.<br /> Fire-Touched - Those who dishonor and disrespect the Hisil.<br /> <br /> So they still get to tag people as sacred prey for arguably arbitrary reasons, since I imagine they get to decide what they feel is appropriate enough dishonor to be worthy of a hunt. Alternatively they seem like they make for good warnings to young werewolves, 'Honor the hunt, pup, or the Predator Kings will find you.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:11:07-07:00","id":436087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436060#post436060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Predator Kings <i>don't</i> hunt the 'weak' as their sacred prey <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The three sacred prey choices of the new Pure are all in their write-up in the Prey section <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be correct to say it like this then?<br /> <br /> Fire-touched: those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow<br /> Predator Kings: those who do not honor the hunt<br /> Ivory Claws: those who do not honor their lineage<br /> <br /> To me these definitions of prey are way to wide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:24:57-07:00","id":436122,"title":"","content":"Hmm, just noticed something. Is Honor not the Ivory Claw tribal renown any more? Only the one in the book hasn't got any dots in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:35:00-07:00","id":436132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435691#post435691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair this is at least partially the book conflating \u201cwolfy\u201d and \u201cspirit\u201d somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; on further review, I got it wrong. The Ivory Claws definitely are the Tribe that needs tools for dealing with high Harmony; the Fire-Touched need means of coping with low Harmony. <br /> <br /> The Predator Kings\u2026 break the wolf/spirit conflation mentioned above. They\u2019re anti-human, which according to the established Breaking Points would drive them toward low Harmony; but they\u2019re not driven toward the Shadow the way the Fire-Touched are. Picking up Bans, having difficulty maintaining a single form, and being biased toward travel into but not out of the Shadow all seem inappropriate for them. They emphasize the wolf in much the same way that the Fire-Born emphasize the spirit. So for them to function properly, you basically need to rewrite the effects of Harmony to reflect Man/Wolf much more than (and possibly even <i>instead of</i>) Flesh/Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:37:19-07:00","id":436134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436122#post436122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, just noticed something. Is Honor not the Ivory Claw tribal renown any more? Only the one in the book hasn't got any dots in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, are the cap on highest Renown and the potential for loss of Renown gone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:37:49-07:00","id":436136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436087#post436087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be correct to say it like this then?<br /> <br /> Fire-touched: those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow<br /> Predator Kings: those who do not honor the hunt<br /> Ivory Claws: those who do not honor their lineage<br /> <br /> To me these definitions of prey are way to wide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They are intentionally wide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:43:01-07:00","id":436163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436122#post436122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, just noticed something. Is Honor not the Ivory Claw tribal renown any more? Only the one in the book hasn't got any dots in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently I don't think the Pure Tribal Renowns are defined in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436134#post436134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, are the cap on highest Renown and the potential for loss of Renown gone?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no cap on having to have your Auspice Renown as your highest, or anything of that sort, no, though a Renown still can't go above 5.<br /> <br /> You can't really lose Renown now; gaining Renown literally causes your spirit to change and transform.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:43:53-07:00","id":436165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436132#post436132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; on further review, I got it wrong. The Ivory Claws definitely are the Tribe that needs tools for dealing with high Harmony; the Fire-Touched need means of coping with low Harmony.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings\u2026 break the wolf/spirit conflation mentioned above. They\u2019re anti-human, which according to the established Breaking Points would drive them toward low Harmony; but they\u2019re not driven toward the Shadow the way the Fire-Touched are. Picking up Bans, having difficulty maintaining a single form, and being biased toward travel into but not out of the Shadow all seem inappropriate for them. They emphasize the wolf in much the same way that the Fire-Born emphasize the spirit. So for them to function properly, you basically need to rewrite the effects of Harmony to reflect Man/Wolf much more than (and possibly even <i>instead of</i>) Flesh/Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, the Predator Kings are caught between the two extremes in a very uncomfortable way.<br /> <br /> This is working as intended; the Predator Kings have always been the Pure tribe with what is arguably the greatest difficulty reconciling themselves with Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:53:43-07:00","id":436200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435579#post435579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a fetish in one of the books that made all a werewolf's non-human forms bigger and nastier?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alpha Skin, yep. Lore of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=435399#post435399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the Predator Kings have a second unique Gift (in addition to Savagery), that includes a Giant Wolf form - I'm not saying bring back Primal Form in its entirety (the changed healing rules for Gauru form make that a bit overkill), but the giant wolf form to hunt other werewolves and humans was a good shtick for them to specialize in.<br /> <br /> Then I'd give them Strength &amp; Stealth as their other two Gifts, since that a) fits very well, and b) lets the Blood Talons and Hunters-in-Darkness maintain a unique specialty each (Rage &amp; Nature).<br /> <br /> <br /> The changes to Harmony means that the whole cycle-of-sin-and-penance and the related Rites need to be completely revamped.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, Primal Form could be a facet of Savagery. It kinda fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T14:17:22-07:00","id":436251,"title":"","content":"Primal Form is not a thing anymore. You can get a thematically close approximate with various merits. Leave it alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T05:25:23-07:00","id":436912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436251#post436251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Form is not a thing anymore. You can get a thematically close approximate with various merits. Leave it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they want to use it for their own game. Be polite, dude. There's no need to be rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T05:34:00-07:00","id":436916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436251#post436251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Form is not a thing anymore. You can get a thematically close approximate with various merits. Leave it alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude... I was just saying that it was possible for the Predator Kings to get it via the Savagery gifts, not that it'd be a PC thing.<br /> <br /> I just happen to think that it would fit if the guys who are all about being the ultimate predators have a form that represents the ultimate predator. The forms as they are now are fragmented, it's obvious they'd try to get a <i>better</i> form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T07:03:31-07:00","id":437006,"title":"","content":"And wich Savagery Facet would it be? Purity, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T08:25:10-07:00","id":437071,"title":"","content":"There is a reason Primal Form as a Facet, whether as one that enhances an existing form or allows access to a new one, does not exist anymore. Because you can get the same effect with the form modifier merits already in the book. Its presence is <i>unnecessary</i>, as the way things are done in the 2e core lets the Pure actually have much easier (and narratively speaking, also more fitting) access to &quot;primal form&quot;, and allows for far more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Primal Form wasn't made as a Facet for second edition, <i>because it is already accounted for, better than it used to be.</i><br /> <br /> And if the Pure tribes are going to have unique abilities or new Gifts that they have affinity for, I'd rather the writers not waste a Facet or particular power bringing back the literal Primal Form. It's kind of pointless, and that space could be used for something more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-11-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:46:15-07:00","id":437131,"title":"","content":"It's even an ancient, historical form of werwolves once took in a meta sense, as long as you put the extra dots in strength and stamina.<br /> <br /> Hello Crinos, it's been a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:18:54-07:00","id":437274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=437071#post437071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a reason Primal Form as a Facet, whether as one that enhances an existing form or allows access to a new one, does not exist anymore. Because you can get the same effect with the form modifier merits already in the book. Its presence is <i>unnecessary</i>, as the way things are done in the 2e core lets the Pure actually have much easier (and narratively speaking, also more fitting) access to &quot;primal form&quot;, and allows for far more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Primal Form wasn't made as a Facet for second edition, <i>because it is already accounted for, better than it used to be.</i><br /> <br /> And if the Pure tribes are going to have unique abilities or new Gifts that they have affinity for, I'd rather the writers not waste a Facet or particular power bringing back the literal Primal Form. It's kind of pointless, and that space could be used for something more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which entitles you to be rude to other people about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:37:38-07:00","id":437290,"title":"","content":"I think I was unnecessarily harsh, but rude that was not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:23:32-07:00","id":437342,"title":"","content":"Being <i>unnecessarily </i>harsh<i> is</i> rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T12:56:34-07:00","id":437400,"title":"","content":"I don't think that's necessarily true. But to be frank, I don't particularly care if I came off as rude, because I said what I thought needed to be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-11-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:24:20-07:00","id":437442,"title":"","content":"We get it.<br /> <br /> Now can we try and stay closer to topic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:23:26-07:00","id":437532,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in the unique rites of the Pure. If there's something I'd want to hear about, it's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T02:58:56-07:00","id":438223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=437006#post437006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And wich Savagery Facet would it be? Purity, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Glory. It's hard to be more glorious than a wolf the size of a small bus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=437071#post437071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a reason Primal Form as a Facet, whether as one that enhances an existing form or allows access to a new one, does not exist anymore. Because you can get the same effect with the form modifier merits already in the book. Its presence is <i>unnecessary</i>, as the way things are done in the 2e core lets the Pure actually have much easier (and narratively speaking, also more fitting) access to &quot;primal form&quot;, and allows for far more flexibility.<br /> <br /> Primal Form wasn't made as a Facet for second edition, <i>because it is already accounted for, better than it used to be.</i><br /> <br /> And if the Pure tribes are going to have unique abilities or new Gifts that they have affinity for, I'd rather the writers not waste a Facet or particular power bringing back the literal Primal Form. It's kind of pointless, and that space could be used for something more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get what you are trying to say here, because other forms can be improved, there is no space for a form that goes above and beyond the Gauru form?<br /> Couldn't you just as well say that because you can enhance Urshul and Dalu you don't need Gauru?<br /> <br /> That said, if Primal Form returns, I'd expect it to be magnificent. Add a size or two from Gauru, 3L weaponry, Add at least two from all attributes... while still keeping the Rage and Primal Fear rules, and so on. It should be <i>scary</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:12:44-07:00","id":438228,"title":"","content":"The problem is it's clearly 5 dot gift tier in a design space that doesn't really have much room for them. Shadow Facets are supposed to only be about 3 dots in power, so unless the Pure get some sort of Moon Gift equivalent there's nowhere to put it. <br /> <br /> Now, maybe something that <i>just</i> gave you an extra point of size per dot of Glory would work. Sort of a flashier version of Warrior's Hide, effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:26:36-07:00","id":438233,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the Pure are just more cagey about their Wolf Gifts. They could use that as a form of justification, 'we're more Pure than you, see we can take on the Wolf Mother's Form', etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:27:25-07:00","id":438270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438228#post438228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is it's clearly 5 dot gift tier in a design space that doesn't really have much room for them. Shadow Facets are supposed to only be about 3 dots in power, so unless the Pure get some sort of Moon Gift equivalent there's nowhere to put it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have it as an entire Wolf gift, with each facet adding to your 'primal form' ability based on renown like everything else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:34:04-07:00","id":438272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438228#post438228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is it's clearly 5 dot gift tier in a design space that doesn't really have much room for them. Shadow Facets are supposed to only be about 3 dots in power, so unless the Pure get some sort of Moon Gift equivalent there's nowhere to put it.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe something that <i>just</i> gave you an extra point of size per dot of Glory would work. Sort of a flashier version of Warrior's Hide, effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's more or less what I'm thinking - I didn't think it would be a true return of Primal Form - like I said, the enhanced Gauru healing the edition already provides makes that overkill. But the menacing aesthetic of a tank-sized wolf for the Predator Kings specifically is not something I think should be thrown out.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not opposed to the Pure getting some 1-5 Gift list of their own... or perhaps more powerful Tribal Merits than the Forsaken get? Something to give them a bit of an edge of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-12-2015, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:38:31-07:00","id":438275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438270#post438270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could have it as an entire Wolf gift, with each facet adding to your 'primal form' ability based on renown like everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that more or less what Strength does now? With a bit of help from Rage, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:45:06-07:00","id":438278,"title":"","content":"Obviously it'll be up to whoever writes the full new Pure rules eventually, but I wouldn't hold my breath waiting for Primal Form to be returned to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:36:29-07:00","id":438326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438275#post438275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that more or less what Strength does now? With a bit of help from Rage, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why if you wanted to homebrew it you'd try to make it more than just about strength or rage. You'd channel Father Wolf and the core of the hunt through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:43:43-07:00","id":438330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438223#post438223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get what you are trying to say here, because other forms can be improved, there is no space for a form that goes above and beyond the Gauru form?<br /> Couldn't you just as well say that because you can enhance Urshul and Dalu you don't need Gauru?<br /> <br /> That said, if Primal Form returns, I'd expect it to be magnificent. Add a size or two from Gauru, 3L weaponry, Add at least two from all attributes... while still keeping the Rage and Primal Fear rules, and so on. It should be <i>scary</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we need the design space of an entire Gift/Facet for what is essentially a glorified super Urshul form. As I said, the form modifier merits serve that purpose well enough, and they don't restrict you to the Urshul direction either - you can invest in a massively improved Gauru form, which is even scarier and would probably fit better than 'Primal Form' for some Pure.<br /> <br /> Someone earlier in the thread suggested just giving the Predator Kings easier access to the relevant merits, and that works just fine. If the writers were so inclined, they could just as easily come up with a merit allowing them to activate the Primal Fear Gauru rules in another hybrid form or just Urshul at the cost of having to deal with the Rage rules as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-12-2015, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T06:46:36-07:00","id":438335,"title":"","content":"I think a supplementary Merit to the other form-adjustment Merits that gives extra Size to Urshul could work for the idea above wherein the Predator Kings have &quot;larger and more magnificent&quot; Urshul shapes.<br /> <br /> Maybe something something that gives +1 to Size and Intimidation for two dots, and +2 to each for 4 dots (and stacks with the basic Huge Merit, which means that you could have a Size 10 Urshul shape. Yiiikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:00:07-07:00","id":438352,"title":"","content":"Actually that's a point. The Favored Form merit mentions the character being &quot;bigger&quot; than normal. Does size count as an attribute for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:10:49-07:00","id":438361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=438335#post438335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a supplementary Merit to the other form-adjustment Merits that gives extra Size to Urshul could work for the idea above wherein the Predator Kings have &quot;larger and more magnificent&quot; Urshul shapes.<br /> <br /> Maybe something something that gives +1 to Size and Intimidation for two dots, and +2 to each for 4 dots (and stacks with the basic Huge Merit, which means that you could have a Size 10 Urshul shape. Yiiikes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed... My 1E Hunter in Darkness Cahalith had a Size 10 Primal Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:28:28-07:00","id":440291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435331-the-pure-2e-style?p=436136#post436136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are intentionally wide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know. I don't question the decision to make them wide, but to make them SO wide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:18:15-07:00","id":450683,"title":"","content":"I'd like to keep the unique gifts from 1e for the Pure. I feel like it was their unique blessing from their extremely close ties to their totems and the spirit world. The Spirits offered them secrets that they did not offer the Forsaken. Not as strong as Auspice gifts (cause 8 again on brawl/weaponry, AMIRITE?), these were signature to their primal totems. <br /> <br /> There were a couple in 1E, Agony, Savagery, Ferver, Disease, and that other Ivory claw one....I forget.....<br /> <br /> I'd do the 4 gift list affinities as:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ivory Claws<br /> Agony, Dominance, Evasion, Warding, <br /> <br /> Fire Touched<br /> Fervor, Inspiration, Knowledge, Elemental<br /> <br /> Predator Kings<br /> Savagery, Stealth, Rage, Nature<br /> <br /> Some idea --<br /> Agony would be something like:<br /> <br /> Cunning - Ideal - make an idea or concept painful, changing an affected targets opinion on it<br /> Honor - cause pain negative to opponents social actions<br /> Wisdom - Use pain to gain visions (like Insight almost...maybe?)<br /> Glory - Taking pain makes you stronger (damage you take or have gives bonus to attack rolls?)<br /> Purity - Attacking you causes pain (reflexive damage, or negatives on next turn? Tilt?)<br /> <br /> Fervor would be something like a mix of the old Fervor and Disease:<br /> <br /> Cunning - disease that causes dreams about a specific topic (wolf as friend, hero, foe etc. visions of religious figures turning into wolves, false prophecies) &quot;I'm the man from your dreams&quot;<br /> Honor - give awe or majesty condition<br /> Wisdom - fevered dreams - see things about a foe <br /> Glory - bonuses in death rage<br /> \u200bPurity - become untouchable if you do not harm foe<br /> <br /> Savagery would be something like the following (all regarding kuruth):<br /> <br /> Cunning - other werewolves in kuruth always sense you in kuruth, even if you are not<br /> Honor - never attack packmates in Kuruth<br /> Wisdom - hide your kuruth resonance from spirits, deal extra damage to spirits when in kuruth<br /> Glory - gain extra triggers for Kuruth<br /> \u200bPurity - Use willpower/essence to end Kuruth early<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm a big Fanboy for the Pure. Something about the religious zealotry mixed with the hard decisions and the way their tribes are so...over the top. Plus, Ivory Claws. I mean, c'mon, right?<br /> <br /> I like my Blood Talons (especially non-stereotypical ones, the Irraka martyr assassin, the half moon war diplomat and my stormlords (the beta, the fetish crafter, the culture scholar, the rising star), stuff like that. And who doesn't love Hunters in Darkness. Or Iron Masters, or, well you get it. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I love to hate the Pure. They are the perfect villains. Ones you can relate to, ones you can hate, but ones you can also respect for being just as badass. That way, when you finally do win (this is our game right? Gotta win. usually.) it feels like a true victory. <br /> <br /> I like using the old bloodline, blueblood and lord noble families of europe with Ivory Claws, the ancient family with dark pasts and high standards that push their children beyond physical and mental lines to be the best. <br /> <br /> Fire Touched that are wise, and a patient, but whisper truths to you that slowly make you realize that they are right. Fire Touched so wild they make skin heads look like geriatric patients. <br /> <br /> Predator Kings that recruit by respecting the forsaken, then brutually murdering them if they do not follow. Predator Kings like shadows in the dark, horrid boogeymen that can come from no where, and are followed by a dozen pack mates. <br /> <br /> I've been doing a lot of work on totems and engim. Using Engim as packmates, bound to the totem same as the Pure, and used to intimidate, scout, research, manipulate, just like a pack member. <br /> <br /> How have you used the Pure? Are you looking to use their 1e gifts, or just give them access to a mix of new Shadow gifts? <br /> <br /> I'm most interested in your Pure packs and totems. Could you share some of that with us? I'm fleshing out the Pure in my chronicle, and I'm building about a dozen packs, as we like to do things BIG. (old Chicago campaign. We've done the Mage, Vampire and Werewolf stories all. This is our 3rd Werewolf story in the setting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:24:37-07:00","id":450697,"title":"","content":"I really don't like unique Shadow gifts. Nothing's stopping a Forsaken from allying with Fever or Disease spirits, or Savagery or Pain. Or tackling Pure totems and forcing them to share gifts rather than be killed like their pack. And if gifts start being held back, the Sacred Hunt becomes a bit of a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:06:13-07:00","id":450776,"title":"","content":"Unique Shadow Gifts don't really work under the new system due to the changes in what Shadow Gifts <i>are</i> and how they are acquired. I'm personally very keen to avoid unique, restricted Shadow Gifts happening at all in 2e, though I have no further control over that now that 2e is out and about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would still expect various Gifts to be Tribally favoured by the Pure - Disease for the Fire-Touched, Agony for the Ivory Claws, etc - but not for these to be solely limited to them. My vision of the Pure grants them <i>other</i> advantages and strengths, some of which can be inferred from what I wrote for them in their Prey write-up in the 2e corebook. Again, obviously how they actually end up is down to Stew and whoever ends up writing more detail on the Pure when their time comes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:47:58-07:00","id":454804,"title":"","content":"I think I see what you mean. I always pictured the pact with spirits that the Pure had granting them greater access to Shadow Gifts, while Mother Luna's blessing granting the powerful auspice gifts and abilities. In the sense of the new rules, I would consider that the Pure gifts were from the Firstborn, and were taught by powerful totems, or through special hunting rites. So they could be learned by Forsaken, but weren't common at all, and couldn't be learned by attacking a disease spirit or a pain spirit. And with a Pure totem, if its pack were killed, I would think it would spit blasphemies at the Forsaken while they tore it apart, not make a deal for gifts and powers. If it were strong enough, they might be able to tear some of the knowledge out, unless it were from a rite. <br /> <br /> With the personal nature of rites, I think they might fit this role better. Of course, this is my personal bias, but I think it adds some mystery and power to the Pure. Naturally, with Auspices and focused packs, the Pure don't usually stand 1 to 1 versus the Forsaken, even with a single unique Shadow Gift. <br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure, maybe when Stew gets a chance to flesh out the Pure, it'll work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}